lag permission, aur `forceDelete` sirf restricted role.\nInterview line: \"Default behavior nahi badalta. Reporting ke liye opt-in `withTrashed()` alag service mein. Jahan soft delete nahi wahan `deleted_at` add karta hoon, lekin purani hard-deleted history audit ya backup se hi aa sakti hai, aur business ko yeh pehle batata hoon.\"\nScenario 3: Queue worker ek hi job kai baar chala raha hai, duplicate payments","l":"s","p":"Senior Laravel Production Scenarios","c":"Senior Laravel Production Scenarios","f":"i","t":["laravel","production","scenario","docker","data","senior"],"s":"n","x":0},{"id":"sc_3","q":"What Laravel features would you use to guarantee idempotency, and why?","a":"Pehle sach: koi bhi ek feature \"guarantee\" nahi deta. Queues at-least-once hain. Guarantee ek se zyada darjon ka mel hai, aur aakhri guarantee database ya provider deta hai.\nPehle wajah dhoondo (duplicates kyun chale): `retry_after` job `timeout` se chhota (F3), worker crash ya deploy beech mein, job ko do baar dispatch kiya gaya, ya payment call ka timeout aur blind retry.\nLayers (andar se bahar):\nPayment provider ka idempotency key (jaise `Idempotency-Key` header): har payment attempt ki ek key (`order-{id}-attempt-{n}`). Retry par provider wohi result deta hai, naya charge nahi. Sab se mazboot layer kyunke paisa wahan katta hai.\nDatabase unique constraint: `payments` table par `provider_reference` ya `(order_id, kind)` unique. Dusri koshish par duplicate-key error, jo sab se pakki rok hai.\nState transition with conditional update: `UPDATE orders SET status='paid' WHERE id=? AND status='pending'` aur affected rows check (0 matlab pehle hi ho chuka).\n`ShouldBeUnique` (+ `uniqueId()`, `uniqueFor`): ek hi key ki job queue mein dobara dispatch hone se rokta hai. Yeh dispatch-level rok hai, processing ke dauran lock jab tak job khatam ya sab attempts fail na hon. Variant `ShouldBeUniqueUntilProcessing` processing shuru hote hi lock chhor deta hai. Lock expire ho sakta hai, isliye akela kaafi nahi.\n`WithoutOverlapping` job middleware: ek hi key par ek waqt mein ek hi job chale (`new WithoutOverlapping($orderId)`), race ke dauran do workers ko rokta hai.\nRetry config: `$tries`, `$backoff`, `$timeout`, aur `retry_after` > timeout, `$failOnTimeout`. Payment jobs ke liye `tries` kam (ya 1) aur failure par reconciliation.\n`afterCommit()`: job tab dispatch ho jab order commit ho chuka ho.\nTransaction + `lockForUpdate()`: order row lock kar ke state check, phir kaam.\nReconciliation job: provider se asal status mila kar `unknown` aur `pending` ko theek karna.\nclass ChargeOrder implements ShouldQueue, ShouldBeUnique {\n    use Queueable;\n    public int $tries = 3;\n    public array $backoff = [30, 120];\n    public int $timeout = 30;                 // retry_after config mein isse bara\n    public int $uniqueFor = 3600;\n    public function __construct(public int $orderId) {}\n    public function uniqueId(): string { return (string) $this->orderId; }\n    public function middleware(): array { return [new WithoutOverlapping($this->orderId)]; }\n    public function handle(PaymentGateway $gateway): void {\n        DB::transaction(function () use ($gateway) {\n            $order = Order::lockForUpdate()->findOrFail($this->orderId);\n            if ($order->status !== 'pending') { return; }              // pehle hi ho chuka\n            $result = $gateway->charge($order, idempotencyKey: \"order-{$order->id}-charge\");\n            $order->update(['status' => 'paid', 'provider_ref' => $result->reference]);\n        });\n    }\n}\nChargeOrder::dispatch($order->id)->afterCommit();\n(Transaction ke andar external call ka nuqsan: DB lock lambi der; behtar: pehle `charging` state commit, phir call, phir `paid`. Is trade-off ka zikr karna senior jawab hai.)\nInterview line: \"Queues at-least-once hain, to idempotency layers se banti hai: provider ka idempotency key, DB ka unique constraint, conditional state update, aur upar se ShouldBeUnique aur WithoutOverlapping. Aakhri guarantee DB aur provider dete hain, Redis lock nahi.\"\nScenario 4: 50 million rows ki table ka column type badalna, downtime allowed nahi","l":"s","p":"Senior Laravel Production Scenarios","c":"Senior Laravel Production Scenarios","f":"i","t":["laravel","production","scenario","docker","data","senior"],"s":"n","x":0},{"id":"sc_4","q":"What migration strategy would you follow in Laravel + MySQL?","a":"Pehle yeh samjho ke seedha `ALTER ... MODIFY` kyun nahi: MySQL mein column ka data type badalna in-place nahi hota, poori table rebuild (copy) hoti hai aur is dauran writes block ho jati hain. 5 crore rows par yeh ghanton ki outage ho sakti hai. (Kuch changes online hote hain: naya column add (INSTANT), index add (INPLACE), VARCHAR ki length ek hadd ke andar barhana; lekin type change nahi.) Safety trick: `ALTER ... ALGORITHM=INPLACE, LOCK=NONE` likho. Agar MySQL is tarah nahi kar sakta to wo error de deta hai, chup chaap table lock nahi karta.\nDo raaste:\nA) Online schema-change tool: `gh-ost` (binary log se, triggers ke baghair) ya `pt-online-schema-change` (triggers se). Wo nayi shadow table banate hain, rows chhote chunks mein copy karte hain, chalte changes ko saath apply karte hain, aur aakhir mein atomic rename (cut-over). Zaroorat: table jitni extra disk, replication lag ki nigrani, throttling, aur pehle staging clone par test.\nB) Expand, migrate, contract (app ke andar, Laravel mein):\nExpand: naya column nullable, naye type ke saath add karo (instant ya online).\n// migration (sirf add, koi rebuild nahi)\nSchema::table('payments', function (Blueprint $table) {\n    $table->decimal('amount_new', 14, 2)->nullable()->after('amount');\n});\nDual-write: naya code deploy jo naye aur purane dono columns likhta hai (observer ya model mutator), taake nayi rows consistent hon.\nclass PaymentObserver {\n    public function saving(Payment $p): void {\n        $p->amount_new = $p->amount;            // dono sync\n    }\n}\nBackfill: purani rows chhote batches mein, idempotent, replication lag dekhte hue ruk ruk kar.\nDB::table('payments')->whereNull('amount_new')->orderBy('id')\n    ->chunkById(5000, function ($rows) {\n        DB::table('payments')->whereIn('id', $rows->pluck('id'))\n            ->update(['amount_new' => DB::raw('amount')]);\n        usleep(200_000);                        // replicas ko saans lene do\n    });\nVerify: `SELECT COUNT() FROM payments WHERE amount_new IS NULL OR amount_new <> amount` ka 0 hona, checksum ya sample comparison.\nSwitch reads: feature flag se nayi column par padhna (pehle chhote hisse par), phir sab par.\nContract: purani column par likhna band, kuch din rollback window, phir alag release mein drop (destructive step kabhi usi release mein nahi, F47). Naam badalna ho to `RENAME COLUMN` MySQL 8 mein online hai lekin app code ke saath coordinate.\nDhyan rakhne ki baatein:\nBackfill ke dauran replication lag, binlog size aur disk ka alert; kam traffic waqt; kill switch (job rok sakein).\nNaye column par index backfill ke baad (ya cut-over se pehle), taake backfill ke dauran writes slow na hon.\nForeign keys, triggers aur views jo is column par depend hon unhein check.\nHeavy ALTER ko normal `php artisan migrate` deploy mein mat chalao (deploy timeout ya lamba block). Alag, control wali process ya tool se chalao.\nProduction-size clone par pehle test aur time naapo.\nRollback plan: purani column cut-over tak chhui nahi hoti, to wapas jana aasan.\nInterview line: \"MySQL mein type change rebuild hota hai aur writes rokta hai, to main ya gh-ost chalata hoon, ya expand-migrate-contract: nayi column, dual-write, batches mein backfill, verify, reads switch, aur purani column alag release mein drop.\"\nScenario 5: Slow aur kabhi kabhi fail hone wali third-party API, users ko random delays","l":"s","p":"Senior Laravel Production Scenarios","c":"Senior Laravel Production Scenarios","f":"i","t":["laravel","production","scenario","docker","data","senior"],"s":"n","x":0},{"id":"sc_5","q":"How would you design a resilient Laravel integration? (timeouts, retries, fallbacks)","a":"Asal wajah delays ki: slow API har request ka FPM worker pakad leti hai (F39). Isliye maqsad: provider ki slowness user tak na pohnche aur hamare workers na phanse.\nDesign ke hisse:\nTimeouts (sab se pehle): connect 1 se 2 second, total user-facing path par 3 se 5 second. Bina timeout ke ek slow call poori site slow kar sakti hai.\nSelective retries: sirf idempotent calls (GET, ya idempotency key ke saath POST) aur sirf transient errors (connection, 5xx), exponential backoff plus jitter, aur total waqt par hadd. 4xx par retry nahi.\nCircuit breaker: lagataar failures par kuch der call hi band (fail fast), provider ko recover hone ka moqa.\nFallback: aakhri theek jawab (stale cache), flat rate ya default, doosra provider, ya \"baad mein confirm hoga\" wali degraded service.\nAsync jahan mumkin: call queue job mein, user ko \"processing\" aur status endpoint (202). User-facing request ko provider par bandhna nahi.\nBulkhead: is provider ke jobs alag queue aur limited concurrency, taake wo baqi kaam na roke.\nRate limiting: provider ki limits ke andar (`RateLimited` job middleware, `Http::pool` mein concurrency).\nAdapter plus validation: provider ki response ko apni DTO mein, shape validate (F45).\nObservability: har call ki duration, status, error rate log aur metrics, aur alert (error rate ya p95 latency).\n// Adapter: timeouts aur selective retry\n$response = Http::timeout(3)->connectTimeout(1)\n    ->retry(2, 200, fn ($e) => $e instanceof ConnectionException, throw: false)\n    ->get($url);\nif ($response->failed()) { throw new ProviderUnavailable($response->status()); }\n// Service: circuit breaker (cache mein) aur fallback\nfinal class ShippingRates {\n    public function __construct(private ShippingApi $api) {}\n    public function quote(Cart $cart): Quote {\n        if (Cache::get('shipping:circuit') === 'open') {\n            return $this->fallback($cart);                          // breaker open: seedha fallback\n        }\n        try {\n            $quote = $this->api->quote($cart);\n            Cache::put(\"shipping:last:{$cart->zone}\", $quote, now()->addHours(6));\n            Cache::forget('shipping:failures');\n            return $quote;\n        } catch (Throwable $e) {\n            report($e);\n            Cache::add('shipping:failures', 0, 60);                 // counter ki 60 second ki umar\n            if (Cache::increment('shipping:failures') >= 5) {\n                Cache::put('shipping:circuit', 'open', now()->addSeconds(30));   // 30 second breaker open\n            }\n            return $this->fallback($cart);\n        }\n    }\n    private function fallback(Cart $cart): Quote {\n        return Cache::get(\"shipping:last:{$cart->zone}\") ?? Quote::flatRate($cart);   // last good ya flat rate\n    }\n}\nQueue jobs ke liye Laravel ka `ThrottlesExceptions` job middleware: baar baar exception par job ko kuch der rok deta hai (ek tarah ka job-level breaker):\npublic function middleware(): array {\n    return [(new ThrottlesExceptions($maxExceptions, $decay))->backoff(5)];\n    // $decay ki unit apne Laravel version ki docs se confirm karein\n}\nInterview line: \"Provider slow ho to hamare workers nahi phansne chahiyein: chhote timeouts, sirf idempotent retries backoff ke saath, circuit breaker, stale-cache ya default fallback, aur jahan ho sake call queue mein. Aur har call ki latency aur error rate par alert.\"\nLaravel Data (Spatie): arrays ki jagah typed DTOs\nLinkedIn post ka naam \"hidden gem\" theek hai, lekin interview mein isay balanced tareeqe se bolna chahiye: faide aur qeemat dono.","l":"s","p":"Senior Laravel Production Scenarios","c":"Senior Laravel Production Scenarios","f":"i","t":["laravel","production","scenario","docker","data","senior"],"s":"n","x":0},{"id":"f_F93","q":"Two admins edit the same record and one silently overwrites the other. How do you prevent it?","a":"Agar conflicts bohat aam hon ya kaam chhota ho to pessimistic `lockForUpdate()` transaction mein. Counters ke liye `increment()` (atomic).","l":"s","p":"Failure-First Backend Interview","c":"Failure-First Backend Interview","f":"i","t":["failure-first","production","resilience","php","laravel","backend"],"s":"n","x":0}]
